          <h3>Complete connection checklist</h3>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Connection</th><th>Cable / wire</th><th>Where it goes</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Battery → Fuse → Splice</td><td>XT60 + 16 AWG</td><td>10 A fuse on the red (+) lead, splice in the right side bay</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Splice → UBEC 1 &amp; UBEC 2 inputs</td><td>16 AWG / XT60</td><td>Front right (UBEC 1, 5.2 V) &amp; front left (UBEC 2, 7.4 V)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>UBEC 1 output → Pi 5</td><td>2-pin Dupont</td><td>Pi pins 4 (5 V) and 6 or 9 (GND) — <i>leave unplugged until step {at("Check the voltages and power up")}</i></td></tr>
              <tr><td>UBEC 2 output → Adapter 1</td><td>16 AWG</td><td>Adapter 1 screw terminal (rear left) — <i>leave unplugged until step {at("Check the voltages and power up")}</i></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Splice → Adapter 2 (direct battery)</td><td>16 AWG</td><td>Adapter 2 screw terminal (rear right) — <i>leave unplugged until step {at("Check the voltages and power up")}</i></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Bus 1 servo chain (7.4 V)</td><td>Molex 5264 3-pin</td><td>Adapter 1 sockets → 4 hips (IDs 3–6), head yaw (2) &amp; head pitch (1)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Bus 2 servo chain (battery)</td><td>Molex 5264 3-pin</td><td>Adapter 2 sockets → left wheel (11) &amp; right wheel (12)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pi 5 → Bus servo adapters</td><td>2× USB-A to USB-C</td><td>Pi USB-A ports → adapter USB-C sockets (adapter switches set to <b>USB</b>)</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pi 5 → OAK-D Lite</td><td>USB 3 (USB-A to C)</td><td>Pi <b>blue</b> USB 3 port → OAK-D Lite rear USB-C</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Pi 5 → LSM6DS3TR-C IMU</td><td>STEMMA QT (&lt; 20 cm)</td><td>Pi pins 1 (3.3 V), 3 (SDA), 5 (SCL), 6 or 9 (GND) → IMU rear socket</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <ol>
            <li>Connect the servo chains: the four hips and two head servos into adapter 1's rear sockets, and the two wheel servos into adapter 2's sockets (the two sockets on each adapter are parallel on that bus, so you can branch or daisy-chain).</li>
            <li>Make sure both USB cables from the Pi are plugged into the adapters, both adapter switches are set to <b>USB</b>, the OAK-D Lite USB 3 cable is in a <b>blue</b> Pi USB 3 port, and the IMU wires match the pinout above.</li>
            <li>Check the power leads from the splice: connect the inputs of UBEC 1 and UBEC 2, and <b>leave both UBEC outputs and both adapters' screw terminals disconnected for now</b> so the next step can check the voltages before anything sees power.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="warn"><b>Never</b> connect battery voltage to adapter 1, and never connect the two servo buses together. The hip and head servos are 7.4 V servos, and a full 3S battery at 12.6 V will destroy them.</p>
        </Step>

        <Step n={32} title={t(32)} parts={ALL} frame="all" image={still(32)} alt="The finished robot, ready for its first power-up.">
          <p>Check the voltages before any servo or the Pi sees them. A UBEC set wrong is the one mistake here that can't be undone.</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Move each leg and the head by hand through their range. Nothing should rub or catch.</li>
            <li>With the UBEC outputs and both adapters' screw terminals still disconnected, connect the battery and measure each UBEC's output with the multimeter: <b>UBEC 1 must read 5.2 V</b> and <b>UBEC 2 must read 7.4 V</b>.</li>
            <li>Disconnect the battery. Now plug UBEC 1 into the Pi's 5 V and ground pins, wire UBEC 2 to adapter 1's screw terminal (+ to +, − to −), and wire the battery-voltage lead from the splice to adapter 2's screw terminal (use the screw terminals, not the DC jacks).</li>
            <li>For the first power-up with the servos connected, plug the <b>6 V bench supply</b> in where the battery goes. If something is miswired, a bench supply limits the damage where a LiPo won't. Bus 1 runs a little under 7.4 V on it, which is fine for these checks.</li>
            <li>Let the Pi draw more current over USB, which the camera needs. Add this line to <code>/boot/firmware/config.txt</code> and restart:
              <pre><code>usb_max_current_enable=1</code></pre>
            </li>
            <li>Check the IMU is on the bus: <code>i2cdetect -y 1</code> must show <code>6a</code>.</li>
          </ol>
        </Step>

        <Step n={33} title={t(33)} parts={ALL} frame="all" image={still(33)} alt="The finished Road Runner Mini.">
          <p>Each step below must pass before you move to the next; the <a href={ROBOT_README}>robot README</a> covers each tool in more detail. Run them from <code>~/roadRunnerMiniV1/robot</code>.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><b>Calibrate.</b> With all servos connected, run <code>.venv/bin/python tools/calibrate.py</code> and follow the prompts. The servos stay limp so you can move them by hand. Hold the robot in the air for the legs and head, then stand it on the floor for the wheels; a phone spirit-level app helps you set the body level.</li>
            <li><b>Check the IMU.</b> <code>.venv/bin/python tools/check_imu.py</code>: all three checks must say OK.</li>
            <li><b>Wheels in the air.</b> Hold the robot up with the wheels free and run <code>.venv/bin/python run_brain.py --air</code> (add <code>--bench-power</code> while on the bench supply). The legs move to the standing pose. Tip the robot forward a little: the wheels must turn forward, trying to drive under the body. Tip it back: they turn backwards. If a wheel turns the wrong way, press q and calibrate again.</li>
            <li><b>Held on the floor.</b> Now on the battery, run <code>.venv/bin/python run_brain.py --held</code>, hold the robot upright on its wheels and press Enter. Keep your hands close without touching it. Press q to stop.</li>
            <li><b>First drive.</b> <code>.venv/bin/python run_brain.py</code>. Keys: w/s speed, a/d turn, r/f height, space to stand still, q to stop. Add <code>--pad</code> to drive with a paired Xbox gamepad, or <code>--depth</code> to let the camera slow it for obstacles.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="warn"><b>It will fall when it stops</b> The program stops the robot if it tips past 35°, if the battery drops to 10.5 V or if a servo stops answering, and the legs go limp. Be ready to catch it, and disconnect the battery when you're done.</p>
        </Step>

        <section class="prep" id="if-something-is-wrong" aria-labelledby="wrong-title">
          <h2 id="wrong-title">If something is wrong</h2>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>What you see</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Do this</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>i2cdetect</code> doesn't show <code>6a</code></td><td>IMU wiring, or I²C not turned on</td><td>Check the four wires against step {at("Fit the IMU plate and the IMU")} and the <code>config.txt</code> line from step {at("Set up the Raspberry Pi")}.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>A wheel turns the wrong way with <code>--air</code></td><td>Calibration recorded the wrong direction</td><td>Stop with q and run <code>tools/calibrate.py</code> again.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>A leg moves the wrong way during calibration</td><td>Two hip servos have swapped IDs</td><td>Unplug them and set their IDs again one at a time with <code>tools/setup_ids.py</code>.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>The robot rocks slowly back and forth</td><td>A loose knee screw</td><td>Check all four knee nuts. Logs from a robot with loose knees don't mean much.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>The program stops saying a servo didn't answer</td><td>Unplugged cable, wrong ID or no power on that bus</td><td>Check the chain on that adapter, its switch (USB) and its screw-terminal power.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>“Battery low” warning</td><td>The pack is at 10.8 V</td><td>Finish up; at 10.5 V the program stops. Charge the battery.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <section class="prep" id="final-checks" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
          <h2 id="checks-title">Final checks</h2>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li>Every insert is flush and straight, and every small screw grips without spinning.</li>
            <li>No gap between any hip servo and its pads in the spine.</li>
            <li>Washers are under the upper-link and rear-link screws, and all four knees swing freely without play.</li>
            <li>The IMU's X arrow points to the nose and the board doesn't move.</li>
            <li>UBEC 1 reads 5.2 V, UBEC 2 reads 7.4 V, and the wheel bus is the only one on battery voltage.</li>
            <li>The legs never touch the tray anywhere in their range, and the head turns ±90° without pulling its cables.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Before every run, check the four knee screws. Something unclear or wrong in this guide? <a href={`${REPO}/issues`}>Open an issue on GitHub</a> so the next builder benefits.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <aside class="viewer-col" aria-label="3D view of the current step">
        <div class="viewer-box">
          <span class="viewer-step" data-viewer-label>Step 1</span>
          <div class="viewer-bar" data-viewer-bar>
            <button type="button" data-viewer-go="-1" aria-label="Previous step">←</button>
            <button type="button" data-viewer-go="1" aria-label="Next step">→</button>
            <button type="button" data-viewer-close>Close</button>
          </div>
          <AssemblyViewer model={MODEL} label="3D view of Road Runner Mini showing the parts for the current step" />
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .guide { padding: 32px var(--gutter) 64px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .intro { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  h1 { font-size: 48px; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .lede { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--quote); }
  .note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 64ch; }

  .layout { display: block; }
  .viewer-col { display: none; }
  .steps { max-width: 68ch; }

  .prep { padding: 32px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: #444; }
  .prep h2 { font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--ink); }
  .prep h3 { font-size: 19px; margin: 20px 0 8px; color: var(--ink); }
  .prep ul { padding-left: 1.3em; margin: 0; }
  .prep li + li { margin-top: .4em; }
  .prep b { font-weight: normal; color: var(--ink); }
  .ideas { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .ideas dt { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 18px; color: var(--ink); }
  .ideas dd { margin: 4px 0 0; }
  .joints { margin-top: 24px; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13px; }
  .joints th, .joints td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .joints th { font-weight: normal; color: var(--muted); }
  .small { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .prep .warn, .prep .tip { margin-top: 16px; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 3px solid var(--heat); background: #fafaf8; }
  .prep .tip { border-left-color: var(--link); }
  .prep .warn b:first-child, .prep .tip b:first-child { font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-right: 6px; }
  .stage { margin-top: 24px; padding: 28px 0 6px; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.15; }
  .stage span { display: block; font: 11px var(--sans); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .stage-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--quote); margin: 4px 0 8px; }
  .rest { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 10px; }
  .rest figure { margin: 0; flex: 1; border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .rest img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .rest figcaption { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); padding: 4px 8px; }
  #if-something-is-wrong table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13px; margin-top: 12px; }
  #if-something-is-wrong th, #if-something-is-wrong td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 8px 10px 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  #if-something-is-wrong th { font-weight: normal; color: var(--muted); }
  #if-something-is-wrong code { font: 12px var(--mono); background: var(--chip); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px; }
  .checks { list-style: none; padding: 0 !important; }
  .checks li { padding-left: 26px; position: relative; }
  .checks li::before { content: "☐"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .diagram { margin: 20px 0; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: #fff; }
  .diagram svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .diagram figcaption { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }

  /* Wide screens: steps on the left, a sticky 3D view on the right that follows the step being read. */
  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .guide.has-viewer .layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(360px, 46%); gap: 48px; align-items: start; }
    .guide.has-viewer .viewer-col { display: block; position: sticky; top: 16px; height: calc(100vh - 32px); max-height: 760px; }
    .guide.has-viewer .map-slot { display: none; }
  }
  .viewer-box { position: relative; height: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .viewer-step { position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 10px; z-index: 2; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--heat); }

  @media (max-width: 600px) { h1 { font-size: 34px; } }

  /* Narrow screens: "View in 3D" on a step opens the same viewer full screen, with step buttons and Close. */
  .viewer-bar { display: none; }
  .guide.is-overlay .viewer-col {
    display: block; position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 50; height: 100dvh; max-height: none; background: #fff;
  }
  .guide.is-overlay .viewer-box { border: 0; }
  .guide.is-overlay .viewer-bar { display: flex; position: absolute; top: 8px; right: 8px; z-index: 3; gap: 6px; }
  .viewer-bar button {
    min-width: 44px; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 14px; font: 14px var(--sans); color: var(--ink);
    background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer;
  }
  .viewer-bar [data-viewer-close] { color: var(--link); border-color: var(--link); }
  .guide.is-overlay .viewer-step { top: 22px; font-size: 13px; }
  :global(html.no-scroll) { overflow: hidden; }

  /* ?capture renders one step at a time for the still pictures (scripts/assembly-stills.mjs). */
  :global(body.capture) .guide > .intro, :global(body.capture) .steps, :global(body.capture .site-header), :global(body.capture .site-footer) { display: none; }
  :global(body.capture) .guide { padding: 0; border: 0; }
  :global(body.capture) .guide .viewer-col, :global(body.capture) .guide.has-viewer .viewer-col { display: block; position: fixed; inset: 0; width: 100vw; height: 100vh; max-height: none; }
  :global(body.capture) .viewer-box { border: 0; }
  :global(body.capture) .viewer-step, :global(body.capture .av-hint), :global(body.capture astro-dev-toolbar) { display: none; }
</style>

<script>
  // Tells the 3D view which step is being read. On narrow screens the view isn't shown or loaded:
  // each step has its own still picture instead.
  const guide = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-guide]")!;
  const capture = new URLSearchParams(location.search).has("capture");
  const wide = matchMedia("(min-width: 1000px)");
  const steps = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-step]")];
  const label = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-viewer-label]")!;
  const list = (s?: string) => (s ? s.split(",").filter(Boolean) : []);
  const stateOf = (el: HTMLElement) => ({
    parts: list(el.dataset.parts),
    focus: list(el.dataset.focus),
    from: el.dataset.from ? (el.dataset.from.split(",").map(Number) as [number, number, number]) : undefined,
    view: el.dataset.view as "front" | "back" | "below" | "left" | "right" | undefined,
    frame: el.dataset.frame as "focus" | "all" | undefined,
  });

  if (capture) {
    document.body.classList.add("capture");
    (window as unknown as { guideSteps: unknown }).guideSteps = steps.map(stateOf);
  }

  let viewer: HTMLElement | null = null;
  let current: HTMLElement | null = null;
  const show = (el: HTMLElement) => {
    if (el === current) return;
    current = el;
    label.textContent = `Step ${el.dataset.step}`;
    document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("assembly-step", { detail: stateOf(el) }));
  };

  // The step being read is the last one whose top has passed 40% of the way down the screen.
  const update = () => {
    const line = innerHeight * 0.4;
    let active = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (s.getBoundingClientRect().top <= line) active = s;
    show(active);
  };

  const start = () => {
    if (viewer || !(wide.matches || capture)) return;
    try { if (!document.createElement("canvas").getContext("webgl2")) return; } catch { return; }
    guide.classList.add("has-viewer");
    viewer = guide.querySelector("assembly-viewer");
    let ticking = false;
    addEventListener("scroll", () => { if (!ticking) { ticking = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { ticking = false; update(); }); } }, { passive: true });
    if (!capture) update();
  };
  start();
  wide.addEventListener("change", start);

  // Narrow screens: each step's "View in 3D" button opens the viewer full screen at that step.
  const hasWebGL = (() => { try { return !!document.createElement("canvas").getContext("webgl2"); } catch { return false; } })();
  const buttons = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-view3d]")];
  const closeButton = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-viewer-close]")!;
  let opener: HTMLElement | null = null;
  const stepEl = (n: number) => steps.find((s) => Number(s.dataset.step) === n);

  const openAt = (n: number, from?: HTMLElement) => {
    const el = stepEl(n);
    if (!el) return;
    if (from) opener = from;
    guide.classList.add("is-overlay");
    document.documentElement.classList.add("no-scroll");
    // The viewer loads the first time it's on screen; replay the step once it's ready so the new parts slide in.
    const v = guide.querySelector<HTMLElement>("assembly-viewer")!;
    current = null;
    show(el);
    if (!v.classList.contains("is-ready")) {
      const wait = setInterval(() => { if (v.classList.contains("is-ready")) { clearInterval(wait); current = null; show(el); } }, 150);
    }
    closeButton.focus();
  };
  const close = () => {
    guide.classList.remove("is-overlay");
    document.documentElement.classList.remove("no-scroll");
    opener?.focus();
  };
  const toggleButtons = () => buttons.forEach((b) => (b.hidden = wide.matches || !hasWebGL));
  toggleButtons();
  wide.addEventListener("change", () => { toggleButtons(); if (wide.matches) close(); });
  buttons.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => openAt(Number(b.dataset.view3d), b)));
  closeButton.addEventListener("click", close);
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-viewer-go]").forEach((b) =>
    b.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const n = Number(current?.dataset.step ?? 1) + Number(b.dataset.viewerGo);
      if (stepEl(n)) openAt(n);
    }),
  );
  addEventListener("keydown", (e) => { if (e.key === "Escape" && guide.classList.contains("is-overlay")) close(); });
</script>
